The header is the first prose paragraph of the chosen comment, so the glob view prints what a file is for:
- A comment whose first prose paragraph is a license notice is passed over for the next comment (`license.rs`); with only a license comment, a file has no header (`license-only.rs`).
- Rows of decoration print nothing and separate paragraphs, so a `/*!` banner's `*` rows and its title's frame aren't printed (`banner.rs`).
- Badges, link definitions, HTML tags, and code fences aren't prose, so the summary comes after them (`badges.rs`, `fence.rs`).
- A one-line plain comment right above code labels that code, not the file (`section.rs`), while one a blank line separates from code, or one of several lines, is still the header (`plain.rs`).
